{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1393 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "5e2c7b91f1eafac88ab489ae66f3e728ec89c1a8a0f7e5aede35c5d4722ac837" :edb/db-before-t 1392 :edb/db-after-t 1393 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534705 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:40:07.219Z" 13194139534705 true] [17592186184180 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304539 13194139534705 true] [17592186184181 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304536 13194139534705 true] [17592186184181 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304543 13194139534705 true] [17592186184181 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304546 13194139534705 true] [17592186184457 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534705 true] [17592186184457 1100 "What is the value of $lim_(x → - ∞)\\arcsin (2x - 1)$?" 13194139534705 false] [17592186184457 1100 "What is the value of ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)?$" 13194139534705 true] [17592186184457 1145 "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/9e2e705cf17a5dca362c23a23e4d10067ff4390a3f9464dddb6745d78986c02a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is $x\\in [0,1].$ This means that $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is undefined outside this interval.\n\nTherefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is undefined." 13194139534705 true] [17592186304536 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304537 13194139534705 true] [17592186304536 1089 "q-302689" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304536 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534705 true] [17592186304536 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2))=$\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304536 1113 #uuid "1ae9b26e-4b4e-5f6f-aa03-3c0a8cc95e5d" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304536 1145 "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/a7e36a5c534a63199ea97985f1301db0c7675adc8fa0d17f33735c61eec9e871.png)\n\nThe domain of   $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty ,$ the graph tends to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304538 13194139534705 true] [17592186304537 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534705 true] [17592186304537 1041 "field-1" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304537 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304538 13194139534705 true] [17592186304537 1110 #uuid "42791177-a301-5ca8-9f3d-016ee9405d10" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304538 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304538 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534705 true] [17592186304538 1111 #uuid "60d51ea8-9598-589f-91db-00b4a3099381" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304539 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304540 13194139534705 true] [17592186304539 1089 "q-339380" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304539 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534705 true] [17592186304539 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5))=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304539 1113 #uuid "301cfe3d-cf46-5095-bff2-984d0168d45b" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304539 1145 "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/25cea33f2fc3a3bcdbc10ca03f93bd6059eb7d0a7dfcda5eb59f6f671387aea3.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5))=2\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304540 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304541 13194139534705 true] [17592186304540 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304542 13194139534705 true] [17592186304540 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534705 true] [17592186304540 1041 "field-1" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304540 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304541 13194139534705 true] [17592186304540 1110 #uuid "12f5a72f-b190-5748-931c-04aa6c33acba" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304541 1034 "\\pi" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304541 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534705 true] [17592186304541 1111 #uuid "3f26a533-08dc-5210-81c6-a68c05b09c0b" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304542 1034 "0" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304542 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534705 true] [17592186304542 1111 #uuid "c78c4d96-d939-5113-916a-53754e85989c" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304543 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304544 13194139534705 true] [17592186304543 1089 "q-339477" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304543 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534705 true] [17592186304543 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304543 1113 #uuid "54e014fa-7fcf-5f0c-af34-9e133e83876b" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304543 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/24f07da42a537ded7916fc2440dcf3ee1ccdfc81c7b027b47e97814fec059f5a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304545 13194139534705 true] [17592186304544 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534705 true] [17592186304544 1041 "field-1" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304544 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304545 13194139534705 true] [17592186304544 1110 #uuid "c657a2d2-7ac9-5c68-bb7b-c3788dff7152" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304545 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304545 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534705 true] [17592186304545 1111 #uuid "70a86eac-72b3-53a4-ab40-babc50728e2e" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304546 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304547 13194139534705 true] [17592186304546 1089 "q-339490" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304546 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534705 true] [17592186304546 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304546 1113 #uuid "f5e4c600-f08d-56a5-b0e5-8154dc0b42bb" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304546 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/68f1ebd0457e0c127f8ed6c979feba58196aa6bb43d97d211efa9b39bc33f637.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\sqrt{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)) & =sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})) \\\\  & =sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304547 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304548 13194139534705 true] [17592186304547 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534705 true] [17592186304547 1041 "field-1" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304547 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304548 13194139534705 true] [17592186304547 1110 #uuid "06e4bd1d-929f-5865-81dd-f24257086327" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304548 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139534705 true] [17592186304548 1103 #